ns but there is this  question which I mentioned of an  extradition treaty with Saudi Arabia  which is not currently in place would I  mean imagining that that was put in  place would that mostly preempt the  utility of getting these individuals out  to Saudi Arabia or would that only deal  with part of the issue well I think that  you know the idea of Saudi Arabian  government agreeing to an extradition  treaty with the United States is just I  mean not even a an idea worth  entertaining it's never going to happen  but clearly the without an extradition  treaty once these individuals are able  to get out of the United States and  return home  there is really no mechanism in place to  have these fugitives brought back to the  US unless they end up going to a country  where the US has an extradition treaty  say one of these individuals goes back  home to Saudi Arabia and then several  years later decides to go on a vacation  in Europe somewhere they could get  picked up and extradited back to the US  that way but otherwise if they get back  to Saudi Arabia for the time being there  seems to be little the u.s. can do if  they don't want to apply political or  diplomatic pressure on the Saudis and  you know up until now they've chosen not  to do that yeah and no indication as  you're suggesting that that piece is  going to change any any time soon really  excellent with that with that point  there I mean the State Department in a  letter to Senator Ron Wyden who's a  senator from Oregon who was asking the  State Department about you know the all  of these Saudis disappearing and  returning home the State Department  wrote Y in the letter a couple of months  ago and essentially said that there was  nothing that they could do about this  they basically said it was a law  enforcement issue not a diplomatic issue  which is false because the State  Department there's a number of things  the State Department could do on this  particular issue but you know the sort  of implicit  from the letter was that they weren't  going to do anything we've been speaking  with Shane Dixon Cavanaugh staff  reporter with The Oregonian in Portland  Oregon Shane really appreciate you  getting us up to speed and continue the  good work on this I really appreciate  your interest in this issue

